remember pokemon cards you could collect  them and use them in battles with other  players  now there's this game called axi  infinity that's built off that same  concept but this time these game  characters are nfts and you can make  real money from owning them axi infinity  is an example of a play to earn game a  new model in online video games that  allows players to generate an income  from earning cryptocurrencies or nfts no  more will the game studios be able to  capture 100 of the revenue so how do  play to earn games work and what can  this model teach us about the metaverse  play to earn is just one percent of the  global video game industry but it has  garnered an enthusiastic community that  believes in the future of nft video  games and its potential to shape the  metaverse gaming's pushed a lot of  industries forward in its time i think  it's going to be the forefront of nfts i  think it's going to be the forefront of  the metaverse the concept of buying  virtual goods in video games isn't new  but play to earn games turn these goods  into nfts which allows players to sell  them for a profit nfts or non-fungible  tokens are essentially digital deeds  that verify that an item is authentic  and unique  axi infinity is one of the more popular  play to earn games it hit its peak in  2021 going from about 38 000 daily  active players in april to 2.5 million  in december according to the company so  how do players make money in this game  one way to earn cryptocurrency is by  winning battles first one to defeat the  other opponent first wins another way is  by selling your game characters to other  players on an nft marketplace  brent vitt who goes by his gamer handle  cairo says he started playing axey  infinity because of the potential to  make money in  uh prior video games that have played  it's the top 0.01 percent that is  getting the money from the game they're  they're playing and winning in all the  tournaments and in this it's anybody and  everybody can come and earn a couple  bucks he says last summer when the value  of the game's cryptocurrency was at its  peak he was making about fifteen hundred  dollars a month from axi infinity about  the same as the monthly income from his  day job in kansas this is just like the  screen that shows me transferring that  the in-game currency into eth meanwhile  axi infinity makes its money mainly  through fees for example it charges a  4.25 fee for every trade made on the  marketplace  so what can play to earn teach us about  running an economy in the metaverse a  virtual realm where people can work play  and shop  first it shows how owning digital assets  as nfts allows people to buy and sell on  a marketplace much like they would on  the stock market  vit says he once flipped an axi game  character on the marketplace for over 4  500  understanding whenever things are like  over and undervalued is like a very very  valuable asset to have in this space axi  infinity says over 4 billion dollars  worth of axes have been traded on the  marketplace to date  sarah needleman a tech reporter for the  wall street journal says players may  choose to hold on to their axes for the  long term but as with all things crypto  it's still too early to tell how  valuable or permanent those assets will  be even if if a game goes away and you  buy something that was made for that  game will it have value down the line  could it work in another game or in some  other virtual environment and that's  just not clear second play to earn shows  how the earning aspect can encourage  people to learn about crypto and nfts  when we look at the player base like  almost 50 of them have never even had a  bank account and are totally new to  crypto this model also incentivizes  current players to educate others about  the space for example in axi infinity  players developed a scholarship program  to recruit new players who may not have  the money to join on their own  axiomfinity says it's run into an issue  of players earning crypto in the game  and then cashing out their earnings  without participating in the marketplace  economy doesn't work if everyone is you  know extracting more value than that is  being come in and i think that people  are kind of missing that point of nfts  in blockchain because they're so focused  on all of the earnings  third many metaverse companies promise  interoperability or the ability to  travel between virtual spaces with the  same virtual assets and some play to  earn games are already experimenting  with this idea to some degree for  example splinterlands a play to earn  card game allows players to trade  digital goods on marketplaces on two  different blockchains that are connected  by a bridge i think over time if there  are ways to take a virtual item that you  earn in a game and use it outside of  that game that might make these items  more valuable because you could use them  perhaps in a work setting if it's  something cosmetic or they could apply  to multiple games axi infinity says it's  looking toward interoperability as well  but it's unclear how safe it is right  now there are so many hacks like bridges  are you know going under all the time  several hundreds if not billions of  dollars have been lost like this  everyone wants to have this like  interoperable metaverse but in reality  kind of getting to that point is going  to be exceedingly difficult  despite its passionate fan base play to  earn has experienced pushback from some  longtime gamers who say this is just  another way for companies to squeeze  money out of them nfts have also been  under fire lately over concerns about  the security of its technology a lot of  nfts have been created based on  copyrighted material or content without  the permission of the actual creators i  think it's possible that there'll be  some sort of government regulation in  the nft space  play to earn is still evolving but some  companies already see it as part of the  future of gaming farmville maker zynga  and assassin's creed creator ubisoft  entertainment are among the first big  publicly traded video game companies to  say they are experimenting with the  strategy it's likely that games will add  nfts because right now they're already  selling virtual goods other game  companies have expressed interest in it  they haven't actually made a move yet as  more video game makers contemplate  adding nfts tech experts say the ability  to buy and sell nfts in the metaverse  will be key putting gamers in an  important role in the metaverse you're  going to see gaming as being an  integral part of the entire ecosystem i  don't think that we go towards a future  where gaming isn't related to  player owned economies and assets that  are tradeable by the players yo let's go  that was super hyped thank you so much i  appreciate it let's go
 

